-- title:
--   Good reduction of X₁(M) at p∤ M, model form
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K'$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField M)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, of the field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 M)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) of $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma_1(M)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A\to L$, with $K'$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A\to L\to K'$. Let $j'\in K'$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the image of $q^{-1}$ times the rational $j$-numerator power series. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, given as an $A$-algebra. Then the structure morphism [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A ↥K' j'`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ — the morphism out of the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the middle chart into $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebras `chartAlg A ↥K' {j'}` and `chartAlg A ↥K' {j'⁻¹}` of $K'$, induced by their two $A$-algebra structure maps — is smooth, and the pullback of this morphism along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $A\to k$ is an integral scheme.
--
--   This is good reduction of $X_1(M)$ at primes not dividing the level (Igusa; Deligne–Rapoport; Katz–Mazur), stated for the two-chart integral model of the $j$-line inside the level-$M$ function field over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$: the model is smooth over the base and its special fibre over an algebraically closed residue field is integral. It feeds the valuation-theoretic description of the completion at the cusp, the construction of the local ring of the special fibre, and the finite étale level-raising statements for $X_1$.
